  "parent": 2504,
  "title": "Proverbs 31:10–31",
  "content": "<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\",\"contentSize\":\"720px\"},\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"top\":\"2.5rem\",\"bottom\":\"4rem\"}}}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\" style=\"padding-top:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4rem\"><!-- wp:html -->\n<figure class=\"saints-chapter-emblem\" data-saints-angel-version=\"2026-09-20\"><img src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/saints-angel-minister-150x150.png\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/saints-angel-minister-150x150.png 150w, /wp-content/uploads/2026/09/saints-angel-minister-300x300.png 300w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 480px) 96px, 112px\" width=\"112\" height=\"112\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"eager\"><figcaption><a class=\"saints-chapter-emblem__role\" href=\"/bible/ministry/#minister\" title=\"The twelve ministerial roles: Minister\">Minister</a><span class=\"saints-chapter-emblem__separator\" aria-hidden=\"true\">·</span><span class=\"saints-chapter-emblem__meaning\">Diligent compassion</span></figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:html -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":1,\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#b3261e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#b3261e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontStyle\":\"normal\",\"fontWeight\":\"400\",\"fontSize\":\"2.6rem\"}}} -->\n<h1 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-color has-link-color\" style=\"color:#b3261e;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;font-size:2.6rem\">Proverbs 31:10–31</h1>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"saints-pericope\"} -->\n<p class=\"saints-pericope\">A Courageous Woman, More Precious Than Costly Stones</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"center\",\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#6b6b6b\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#6b6b6b\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"15px\"}}} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-text-color has-link-color\" style=\"color:#6b6b6b;font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://staging-8e0d-waywardnightjars.wpcomstaging.com/bible/wisdom/proverbs/chapter-29/\">← Proverbs 29</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href=\"https://staging-8e0d-waywardnightjars.wpcomstaging.com/bible/wisdom/proverbs/\">Proverbs: all chapters</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href=\"https://staging-8e0d-waywardnightjars.wpcomstaging.com/bible/wisdom/ecclesiastes/chapter-1/\">Ecclesiastes 1 →</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"center\",\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#8a8a8a\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#8a8a8a\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"14px\"}}} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-text-color has-link-color\" style=\"color:#8a8a8a;font-size:14px\">Proverbs is read here in the order of the Greek text: chapters 1–24:22, then 30:1–14, 24:23–34, 30:15–33, 31:1–9, chapters 25–29, and 31:10–31.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v31-10\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v31-10\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">31:10</span>A courageous woman—who will find her? Such a woman is more precious than costly stones.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v31-11\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v31-11\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">31:11</span>Her husband’s heart is confident in her; such a woman will not lack fine spoils.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v31-12\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v31-12\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">31:12</span>For she works good things for her husband throughout her life.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v31-13\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v31-13\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">31:13</span>Spinning wool and flax, she made useful work with her hands.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v31-14\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v31-14\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">31:14</span>She became like a ship trading from afar, and she gathers her livelihood.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v31-15\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v31-15\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">31:15</span>And she rises in the night and gave food to the household and tasks to the maidservants.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v31-16\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v31-16\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">31:16</span>After inspecting a farm she bought it, and from the fruits of her hands she planted an estate.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v31-17\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v31-17\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">31:17</span>Having girded her waist strongly, she braced her arms for work.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v31-18\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v31-18\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">31:18</span>She tasted that working is good, and her lamp is not extinguished throughout the night.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v31-19\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v31-19\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">31:19</span>She stretches her forearms toward profitable things, and braces her hands on a spindle.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v31-20\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v31-20\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">31:20</span>She opened her hands to a needy person and stretched out her wrist to a poor person.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v31-21\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v31-21\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">31:21</span>Her husband is not anxious about those at home when he stays away somewhere, for all those with her are clothed.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v31-22\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v31-22\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">31:22</span>She made double cloaks for her husband, and garments of fine linen and purple for herself.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v31-23\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v31-23\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">31:23</span>Her husband becomes distinguished in the gates when he sits in council with the elder inhabitants of the land.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v31-24\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v31-24\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">31:24</span>She made linen cloths and sold them, and girdles for the Canaanites.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v31-25\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v31-25\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">31:25</span>She opened her mouth attentively and lawfully and prescribed order for her tongue.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v31-26\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v31-26\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">31:26</span>She clothed herself in strength and dignity and rejoiced in the last days.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v31-27\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v31-27\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">31:27</span>The occupations of her houses are secure, and she did not eat idle food.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v31-28\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v31-28\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">31:28</span>She opens her mouth wisely and according to law, and her mercy raised up her children, and they became wealthy, and her husband praised her:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v31-29\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v31-29\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">31:29</span>“Many daughters acquired wealth, many did mighty things, but you stand above and have surpassed them all.”</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v31-30\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v31-30\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">31:30</span>A woman’s pleasing qualities are false and beauty is vain; for an understanding woman is blessed, and let her praise the fear of the Lord.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v31-31\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v31-31\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">31:31</span>Give her from the fruits of her hands, and let her husband be praised in the gates.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"center\",\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#6b6b6b\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#6b6b6b\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"15px\"}}} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-text-color has-link-color\" style=\"color:#6b6b6b;font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://staging-8e0d-waywardnightjars.wpcomstaging.com/bible/wisdom/proverbs/chapter-29/\">← Proverbs 29</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href=\"https://staging-8e0d-waywardnightjars.wpcomstaging.com/bible/wisdom/proverbs/\">Proverbs: all chapters</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href=\"https://staging-8e0d-waywardnightjars.wpcomstaging.com/bible/wisdom/ecclesiastes/chapter-1/\">Ecclesiastes 1 →</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n\n<!-- wp:html -->\n<section class=\"saints-english-wording-notes\" style=\"margin-top:2rem;padding:1rem;border-top:1px solid #d5c8af\"><h2 style=\"font-size:1.35rem\">Saints English wording notes</h2><details class=\"saints-english-note\"><summary>Proverbs 31:10 · courageous</summary><p><strong>Sense.</strong> A woman characterized by courage or strength of character.</p><p>Retain courageous or valiant with capable as a contextual connection. Preserve the broad commendation; virtuous should not be narrowed to sexual reputation or domestic compliance alone.</p><p><strong>Historical comparison.</strong> KJV and Brenton have virtuous; DRC valiant. The Greek compares her with costly stones without specifying KJV rubies.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/PRO.31\">Rahlfs–Hanhart Greek chapter</a> · Lexical record carried forward from the Saints Biblical Lexicon, Wisdom review, 26 September 2026. Independent linguistic review remains outstanding.</p></details></section>\n<!-- /wp:html -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#8a8a8a\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#8a8a8a\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"14px\"}}} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" style=\"color:#8a8a8a;font-size:14px\">Bespoke Saints English Translation · 14 October 2026 · Provisional editorial edition awaiting specialist review.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:html -->\n<aside class=\"bespoke-current-notes\" aria-label=\"Current Bespoke editorial notes\" style=\"font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;border-top:1px solid #d4c6ad;margin-top:2rem;padding-top:1rem\"><h2>Current Bespoke editorial notes</h2><p>The newer Bespoke Saints English (1).pdf governs, with accepted Genesis 1–11 as the English benchmark. It supersedes the older Founding Style Guide where their pronoun rules conflict: Thou/Thee/Thy address God directly; ordinary address uses you/your.</p><p>Preserve both separated source blocks, God-spoken oracle without adding Lemuel, repeated What questions and counsel/wine language. Ordinary address to the son and woman uses you/your. Give in 6 and 31 addresses a plural audience, unlike the singular opening commands. Preserve courageous with its inherited note, mixed present/past verbs, Canaanites, 25–26 order, houses plural in 27, expanded 28 and husband praised in 31.</p><p>Greek consultation in this revision: Publisher’s full displayed running text read in the browser for this chapter, with focused comparison of the features listed. No printed apparatus or manuscript collation. Rahlfs–Hanhart 2006 remains the user-authorized provisional base. Focused checks of the publisher’s Greek running text are recorded by chapter. This is an English editorial revision, not a complete critical-text or apparatus verification. Göttingen, full apparatus, independent Greek and human read-aloud reviews remain pending.</p><p>Further review: Review the oracle syntax in 1–2, belated counsel in 3, mixed tenses throughout the woman’s poem, secure occupations in 27 and praise of the husband in 31. Independent Greek, Göttingen/apparatus and human read-aloud review pending.</p></aside>\n<!-- /wp:html -->\n</div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->"
}
